## Context

Experiment 3 (the prompt-composition ablation, `\label{sec:exp3}` in
`report/inputs/plan_ablation.tex`) is an abandoned pilot. The file itself labels
its results *"Résultats pilotes (design initial, invalidés)"* (line ~548) and the
underlying arms were never committed to the scientific record: the
`prompt_version` tag that distinguished the **base** vs **census** arms was
dropped in the mart rebuild (0297/0344), so its figures
(`fig_base_vs_census`, `fig_census_direct`) can no longer be regenerated — they
crash or render an empty 0-model placeholder.

Decision (2026-05-27, MHD): **remove the whole ablation thread** rather than
recover or freeze it. "Ablate ablation." This also unblocks 0352 — the
unbuildable ablation figures were that ticket's wall; deleting them shrinks its
migration inventory to regenerable artifacts only.

Talk-safety: the 2026-05-27 talk is slides-driven. `fig_ablation_strip`/`heatmap`
are **not** `\includegraphics`'d in `slides.tex` (Makefile-only / orphan), so this
removal barely touches the deck — see the keep/flag note below.

## Scope — kill-closure

**Prose / structure (report.tex):**
- Delete `report/inputs/plan_ablation.tex` entirely (the whole §Expérience 3).
- Remove its include: `report.tex:244 \input{inputs/plan_ablation}`.
- Rewrite the **three** forward-references to `sec:exp3` (report.tex ~219, ~236,
  ~242) so Exp1/Exp2 no longer promise an ablation: drop the
  "isole systématiquement l'effet de chaque composant", "condition de contrôle
  externe dans l'expérience d'ablation", and "régime de l'étude d'ablation"
  clauses. The paper becomes a 2-experiment paper. Leave no dangling `\ref`.

**Artifacts (delete file + every Makefile rule/target token):**
- base-vs-census: `report/inputs/generated/{fig_base_vs_census.pdf,
  tab_base_vs_census.tex}`, `src/aedist/{plot_base_vs_census.py,
  tabulate_base_vs_census.py}`, `tests/{test_plot_base_vs_census.py,
  test_tabulate_base_vs_census.py}`.
- ablation figs: `report/inputs/generated/{fig_ablation_strip.pdf,
  fig_ablation_heatmap.pdf}`, the `$(SLIDE_GEN)/fig_ablation_strip.pdf` rule,
  `src/aedist/plot_ablation.py` (+ any test).
- `experiments/models_ablation_p2_rag.yaml`.
- Makefile rules to delete: `P1_BASE_RECORDS` (~67), `tab_base_vs_census` (~69),
  `fig_base_vs_census` (~91), `fig_ablation_strip` (~190 + ~194),
  `fig_ablation_heatmap` (~198); strip ablation tokens from `tables:` (~256),
  `figures:` (~257), and the report.pdf prereq list (~228, ~233).

**Also remove the stale Exp1 census figure** (same dropped-tag root cause, MHD
said it goes): the figure block at `report.tex` ~136–141 (`fig_census_direct`) and
its Makefile rule (~160). **KEEP** the §exp1 prose, `tab_census`, `census_bars`,
and `macros_census` — those are Exp1/slides, regenerable, not ablation. No `\ref`
to `fig:census-direct`, safe.

## Decision needed during execution (flag, default = KEEP)
`fig_direct_p1_base.pdf` + `macros_p1_base.tex` appear in the **slides**
(`slides.tex:114`, `:17`) and derive from `EXP1_BATCH2_RECORDS`, not the ablation
sweep — likely an **Exp1** result, not Exp3. Default: **keep** (and keep Makefile
rule ~168 + `macros_p1_base`). Only remove if MHD rules the p1_base slide is part
of the ablation.

## Optional (defer unless asked)
342 archived raw files under `experiments/archive/outputs/ablation/` — harmless;
leave unless a purge is requested.

## Test (first)
`tests/test_no_ablation_residue.py` (`@pytest.mark.adherence`):
```python
def test_no_ablation_residue():
    # grep the live tree (exclude tickets/, experiments/archive/)
    needles = ["sec:exp3", "plan_ablation", "base_vs_census",
               "fig_ablation_", "plot_ablation", "models_ablation"]
    hits = grep_tree(needles, include=["report/**/*.tex", "slides/*.tex",
                                       "Makefile", "src/aedist/*.py"])
    assert hits == [], f"ablation residue: {hits}"

def test_no_dangling_refs():
    # every \ref/\Cref target resolves to a surviving \label
    assert unresolved_refs("report/report.tex") == []
```

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `plan_ablation.tex` deleted; `\input` removed; 3 `sec:exp3` refs rewritten; no dangling `\ref`
- [ ] all base-vs-census + ablation figures/tables/scripts/tests removed
- [ ] Makefile carries no rule or target token for any removed artifact
- [ ] `fig_census_direct` figure + rule removed; §exp1 prose + `tab_census` kept
- [ ] `fig_direct_p1_base`/`macros_p1_base` fate ruled (default keep)
- [ ] `make report` and `make slides` both build; `make -n report` references no removed artifact
- [ ] `make check` passes; `test_no_ablation_residue.py` green
